---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout 
  title="A-Level Physics Formula Sheet | Mechanics, Waves, Fields"
  description="Complete A-Level Physics formula sheet with mechanics, waves, and fields formulas. Free download for A-Level Physics students."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>A-Level Physics<br><span>Formula Sheet</span></h1>
    <p>Mechanics, waves, and fields formulas. From kinematics to electromagnetism.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Mechanics</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Kinematics</h3>
        <pre><code>v = u + at
s = ut + ½at²
v² = u² + 2as
s = ½(u + v)t</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Forces</h3>
        <pre><code>F = ma
W = mg
F = kx (Hooke's law)
p = mv (momentum)</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Energy</h3>
        <pre><code>KE = ½mv²
PE = mgh
Work = Fd cos θ
Power = W/t = Fv</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Waves</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Wave Equations</h3>
        <pre><code>v = fλ
T = 1/f
v = √(T/μ) (string)
v = √(B/ρ) (fluid)</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Optics</h3>
        <pre><code>n₁ sin θ₁ = n₂ sin θ₂
1/f = 1/v + 1/u
M = -v/u (magnification)</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Fields</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Gravitational</h3>
        <pre><code>F = GMm/r²
g = GM/r²
PE = -GMm/r</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Electric</h3>
        <pre><code>F = kQq/r²
E = F/q = kQ/r²
V = Ed (uniform field)
C = Q/V = ε₀A/d</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Magnetic</h3>
        <pre><code>F = BIL sin θ
F = Bqv sin θ
EMF = -N dΦ/dt (Faraday)</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Download</h2>
    <p>Print this page or save as PDF for quick reference.</p>
    <p><strong>Tip:</strong> Use Ctrl+P (Cmd+P on Mac) to print or save as PDF.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>
